From ff03fae6a4b21b603911b0b56a0253a1cb40b8ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Wu <eric3u@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:13:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] MdeModulePkg: Add Simplified Chinese strings

Translate the setup UI into Simplified Chinese (zh-Hans): the front page,
Boot Manager, Boot Maintenance Manager, Device Manager, Boot Discovery
Policy, the display engine with its key help and pop-ups, the file
explorer and the RAM disk configuration.

Every string of these files gets a zh-Hans entry, including the few that
stay as they are: key letters the code matches input against, such as
"Y (y)", as well as empty and placeholder strings. StrGather leaves a
string a language does not define out of that language's package, and
HiiGetString() does not fall back to another language for it, so a
missing entry would show up as "!" or not at all.

Hanzi carry \wide and \narrow markers. The display engine and the
console take a character's width from them rather than from its glyph.

Signed-off-by: Eric Wu <eric3u@outlook.com>
---
 .../Application/UiApp/FrontPageStrings.uni    |  29 ++++
 .../BootDiscoveryPolicyUiLibStrings.uni       |   5 +
 .../BootMaintenanceManagerStrings.uni         | 137 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../BootManagerUiLib/BootManagerStrings.uni   |  10 ++
 .../CustomizedDisplayLib.uni                  |  19 +++
 .../DeviceManagerStrings.uni                  |  21 +++
